# Copy to wifi.conf on the BENCHDATA partition. NEVER commit the real file: it holds a PSK.
# usb-setup.sh reads it to bring the link up before anything else, because results shipping,
# package installation and remote access all depend on it.

SSID="your-ssid"
PSK="your-passphrase"

# Regulatory domain, as an ISO country code. This matters more than it looks on the 9380's QCA6174:
# under the default world domain (00) most 5 GHz channels are passive-scan only, so association to a
# 5 GHz AP can fail with no obvious error while 2.4 GHz works. Set it to where the machine actually
# is.
COUNTRY="GB"

# Optional. Leave empty to let NetworkManager choose. Pinning the BSSID avoids roaming mid-sweep,
# which shows up as a burst of firmware activity inside a measured window.
BSSID=""

# Optional: a host to ship results to between rounds, as user@host:/path. Shipping happens between
# rounds and never inside a measured window.
RESULTS_REMOTE=""
